n class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Mem.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.5.18</span> </span> (pl.); <span class=\"gk\">ἐ. τῶν παίδων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">12(1).43</span> </span> (Rhodes); <span class=\"gk\">τῶν ἐφήβων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Inscr.Prien.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">112.73</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">(i B.C.)</span>: voc. <span class=\"gk\">ἐπιστάτα</span>, <abbr>=</abbr> <b class=\"lex-tr\">Rabbi, Ev.</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Luc.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.5</span> </span>, al. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">III</span>. <b class=\"lex-tr\">president</b> of a board or assembly: at Athens, <span class=\"gk\">ἐ. τῶν πρυτάνεων</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">chairman</b> of <span class=\"gk\">βουλή</span> and <span class=\"gk\">ἐκκλησία</span> in cent. v, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Arist.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ath.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">44.1</span> </span>, later, <b class=\"lex-tr\">keeper</b> of Treasury or Archives, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.841</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"gk\">ἐ</span>. <span class=\"gk\">τῶν προέδρων</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">chairman</b> of <span class=\"gk\">βουλή</span> and <span class=\"gk\">ἐκκλησία</span> from cent.iv, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Aeschin.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.39</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">22.9</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"gk\">ἐ. ὁ ἐκ τῶν προέδρων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">22